@attribute [Route(GlobalValues.Path_Toggle_Tip_Overview)]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Page_Title_Toggle_Tip_Overview_Test</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Toggletip Overview & Tests</h1>

    <p>
        The Toggletip component is a simple component based on the original idea by Heydon Pickering of a way of showing supplemental information that is revealed on click rather than on hover.
    </p>
    <p>
        The implementation I chose was that of simple disclosure pattern using the new HTML popover attribute so the component has light dismiss on mouse click, has no focus trap and will remain 
        open until closed explicity with the <kbd>Escape</kbd> key or an additional close button and/or opening another item that uses the popover api.
    </p>
    <p>
        The toggletip has also been designed so it can be part of a paragraph of text with the label and icon aligning and sizing to the text.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong>I have used the new css anchor positioning properties which only became base line at the start of the year (2026). 
        I choose not to add the free polyfill by 'oddbird' for older browsers which you can obtain from here: <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" target="_blank" href="https://github.com/oddbird/css-anchor-positioning">https://github.com/oddbird/css-anchor-positioning (opens inert new window)</a>
        so dependant on the age of your browser the popover may just appear top left of the screen instead of being positioned top center of the icon (one of the available component positioning options), but funtionally it will work correctly irrespective of the positioning. 
    </p>
    <p>
        <b>Released: </b>Current version <b>v1.0.1</b> See the documentation site for more information: <a target="_blank" class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Site_Link_Docs_ToggleTip">Toggletip documentation (opens in new window)</a>
    </p>
</section>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h2 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Information & instructions</h2>
    <p>
        You should be able to open and view the toggletip information by activating the components with either the mouse (on either the label or icon), the <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd> key
        on the keyboard (when focused on the icon), or via voice commands by saying the controls accessible name, the label that appears to the left of the toggletip, in this configuration.
    </p>
    <p>
        You should be able to close the toggletip by either using the <kbd>Escape</kbd> key, activing the trigger again, clicking outside of the toogletip with the mouse, pressing the additional
        Close button that has been added or voice control users may re-say the accessible name or the close buttons accessible name (Close Keyboard Info).
    </p>
    <p>
        You should be able to scroll scollable data using the arrow keys.
    </p>
    <p>
        The annoucement history dialog also uses the popover api, so that can be used to test closing of the toggletip via opening of another item that uses the popover api.
        The non-modal <b>Announcement History dialog</b> can be accessed at any time using the keyboard shortcut <span class="br-visually-hidden">Control plus Shift plus the H key</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>H</kbd></span> or by pressing the <b>Alerts button</b> located at the bottom-right
        of the screen.
    </p>
    <h3 id="toggletip-keyboard" class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Keyboard interaction</h3>
    <ul aria-labelledby="toggletip-keyboard">
        <li><kbd>Space</kbd> - when focus is on the toggletip icon, expands or collapses the content.</li>
        <li><kbd>Enter</kbd> - when focus is on the toggletip icon, expands or collapses the content.</li>
        <li><kbd>Escape</kbd> - closes the toggletip</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h3 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Expectations</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>
            The toggletip should show its contents once activated via your chosen activation method.
        </li>
        <li>
            You should be able to tab to the content area and scoll any scrollable data.
        </li>
        <li>
            Tabbing out of the toggletip should go to the next focusable element on the page with the toggletip remaining open.
        </li>
        <li>
            The toggletip should close if the <kbd>Escape</kbd> key is pressed at any time whilst on the page. If focus is on the toggletip then focus should return to the trigger (the icon).
        </li>
        <li>
            The toggletip should close if the "Close Keyboard Info" button is pressed with the focus returning to the trigger (the icon).
        </li>
        <li>
            The toggletip should remain open until explicity closed, you leave the page or another item using the popover api is used.
        </li>

        <li>
            Screen readers should announce that the toggletip is either expanded or collapsed on focus and activation.
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>
